linkpage — third-party notices
==============================

linkpage itself is MIT licensed; see LICENSE.

This file covers the artwork vendored into `packages/renderer/src/icons.ts`. The renderer
declares no dependencies (SPEC.md §5.1), so it cannot import an icon library — every glyph it
uses is copied into its source, and this file is where those copies are attributed.

Two consequences worth stating plainly, because they are the reason these particular sources
were chosen (SPEC.md §2.4):

  * **Font Awesome Free was specifically avoided.** Its CC BY 4.0 licence attaches an
    attribution obligation that would follow every page linkpage exports, onto every site
    those pages are published to. Nothing an owner exports from this tool carries an
    attribution requirement.

  * **Nothing below requires attribution in an exported `index.html`.** ISC and MIT ask that
    their notice accompany copies of *the software*, which this file provides for this
    repository; CC0 asks for nothing. The exported page is the owner's, outright.


